# Copy to .env.local for local development. .env.local is gitignored.
#
# Only one variable is needed. Firebase config is not here — it is committed in
# src/firebase.ts, which is fine: web SDK config is public by design.

# Cloudflare Worker that proxies Gemini for the "Read from image" feature.
# Deploy it from cf-worker/ with:
#   npx wrangler deploy
#   npx wrangler secret put GEMINI_API_KEY
# then paste the resulting URL here.
#
# Leave unset to develop without image reading — the rest of the app works and
# the reader shows a configuration message instead of failing oddly.
#
# The production value is set in .github/workflows/deploy.yml.
VITE_IMAGE_PROXY_URL=https://quoteapp-image-reader.<your-account>.workers.dev

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DO NOT PUT ANY AI API KEY IN THIS FILE OR IN .env.local
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Not OPENROUTER_API_KEY, not GEMINI_API_KEY. Two independent reasons:
#
# 1. It would not work. These files are read by Vite, which builds the
#    FRONTEND. The Cloudflare Worker is a separate program on a separate
#    machine and never sees them.
#
# 2. It would leak the key. Anything Vite exposes is compiled into the public
#    JS bundle and served to every visitor, and this repo is public. That is
#    the exact thing the Worker exists to prevent — the key lives in the
#    Worker's environment so it never reaches a browser.
#
# Keys are Worker secrets. From cf-worker/:
#
#   npx wrangler secret put OPENROUTER_API_KEY
#   npx wrangler secret put GEMINI_API_KEY
#
# It prompts for the value and stores it encrypted at Cloudflare. It is never
# written to disk and never committed.
#
# Which provider/model to use is NOT secret and lives in cf-worker/wrangler.toml
# under [vars] — AI_PROVIDER and OPENROUTER_MODEL.
